  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI made my Apple iCloud Calendar public so that the Homarr calendar widget could display it through the iCal integration. It worked at first, but the next day it started returning an error:\n\nTRPCClientError: An unknown error occurred while executing the Integration method.\n\nI investigated the issue and found that Apple may block the feed after too many requests, which makes the integration unusable in its current form. If I make another iCloud calendar public and integrate that one instead, it works again, but it gets blocked after a day as well.\n\nAdditionally, recurring events do not appear at all.\n\n<img width=\"376\" height=\"375\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/099f6d10-4cb5-4851-8d5f-51eba2035ebe\" />\n<img width=\"968\" height=\"162\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c464db2b-e279-4d05-ba93-c503e1b3c24d\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd an iCloud calendar and wait a day.\n\n### Impact\n\nThe impact is significant \u2014 in its current state it\u2019s essentially unusable. As far as I know, there\u2019s no reliable workaround beyond temporarily switching to another public iCloud calendar, which also gets blocked after a short time.\n\n### Additional information\n\nZen browser\n\n### Version\n\n1.44.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nPortainer\n\n### Browser\n\nOther (describe in \"additional information\")",
